y 49 people. Revenue per employee of $1.9M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue falling 21%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $880K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $75K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["SIGA Technologies Inc. is a micro-cap healthcare business with a $197M market cap on $95M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -7.1pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 102% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 92-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $43M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 46 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.87\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 21.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 43% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -7.1pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 25% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 84% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 187% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Healthcare \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"